From: Neutron
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: WaitForVBlank sleeps until the vertical blank instead of spinning

Mister Horse Product Manager 3.7.7 (JUCE 8) kept 40% of a core busy while idle on its Welcome screen. JUCE 8 runs a
vblank thread that calls IDXGIOutput::WaitForVBlank in a loop. DXVK emulates the wait with Sleep::sleepUntil, which
spins for the last 4 timer periods plus a sixth of the wait: Wine reports a 1 ms timer, so 4 ms + 2.8 ms of every
16.7 ms frame were a busy loop (41% of a core at 60 Hz).

Windows blocks WaitForVBlank in the kernel until the vertical blank (D3DKMTWaitForVerticalBlankEvent); the waiting
thread uses no CPU. The emulated wait now computes the same target time and sleeps the whole wait with
NtDelayExecution; Wine wakes it well within a millisecond. The target (the next refresh boundary after the last
mode change) is unchanged.

Lab, 11.10-183m (183rc + this + dxvk 0007), Product Manager idle, 15-20 s windows: ProductManager.exe 0.6%, 0.7%,
1.0% of a core (3 runs); NEUTRON_DXVK_VBLANK_SPIN=1 on the same build: 40.7% (1 run; mhpm on 182/183rc: 39-40%,
4 runs). Topaz Photo 1.7.1 at its sign-in screen calls WaitForVBlank too: 21.0% here (n=1), 56% on 183rc (smoke183,
n=2; attribution to this patch INFERRED, no kill-switch arm). Not covered: the wait is still an estimate from the
mode's refresh rate, not the display's real vblank.

Kill switch NEUTRON_DXVK_VBLANK_SPIN=1 (the spinning wait). build-external.sh's dxgi_switches must list it.

diff --git a/src/dxgi/dxgi_output.cpp b/src/dxgi/dxgi_output.cpp
index 8814f5cb..a60f0620 100644
--- a/src/dxgi/dxgi_output.cpp
+++ b/src/dxgi/dxgi_output.cpp
@@ -487,8 +487,34 @@ namespace dxvk {
 
     m_monitorInfo->ReleaseMonitorData();
 
-    // Sleep until the given time point
-    Sleep::sleepUntil(t1, t2);
+    // NEUTRON: Windows blocks WaitForVBlank in the kernel until the vertical blank; the thread uses no CPU.
+    // Sleep::sleepUntil spins for the last 4 timer periods plus a sixth of the wait (4 ms + 2.8 ms of each
+    // 16.7 ms frame under Wine's 1 ms timer), and an app with a vblank thread (JUCE 8: Mister Horse Product
+    // Manager) kept 40% of a core busy while idle. Sleep the whole wait instead; Wine's NtDelayExecution wakes
+    // well within a millisecond. Kill switch NEUTRON_DXVK_VBLANK_SPIN=1 (the spinning wait).
+    static const bool s_spin = env::getEnvVar("NEUTRON_DXVK_VBLANK_SPIN") == "1";
+
+    if (s_spin) {
+      Sleep::sleepUntil(t1, t2);
+      return S_OK;
+    }
+
+    using NtDelayExecutionProc = LONG (WINAPI*)(BOOLEAN, PLARGE_INTEGER);
+    static auto s_delay = reinterpret_cast<NtDelayExecutionProc>(reinterpret_cast<void*>(
+      ::GetProcAddress(::GetModuleHandleW(L"ntdll.dll"), "NtDelayExecution")));
+
+    auto now = dxvk::high_resolution_clock::now();
+
+    if (t2 > now) {
+      LARGE_INTEGER ticks;
+      ticks.QuadPart = -std::max<int64_t>(1, std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(t2 - now).count() / 100);
+
+      if (s_delay)
+        s_delay(FALSE, &ticks);
+      else
+        Sleep::sleepUntil(now, t2);
+    }
+
     return S_OK;
   }
   
